=== initial-brainstorming.md ===
* Markov matrices, steady states
* chaotic attractors: cyclical non-repeating processes
* iterative simulation refinement, newton's method (?)
* vertical and horizontal causality (alex o'connor). two entities can have a dependency where one requires the sustained existence of another, i.e. an apple sitting on a desk requires the desk to exert electromagnetic forces on the apple (in addition to existence of gravity opposing the electromagnetic force to cause it to be static). two entities can also be sequential; canonically a temporal dependency, alex's canonical example is toppling dominoes. an earlier domino can be reset without changing the overall effect of the chain of dominoes being toppled. more relevant to investing: an effect could be due to any number of causes and looking for any particular cause, even if that cause was the particular cause of the effect, it could be undone or otherwise unmeasurable
* cellular automata (wolfram, conway). procedural generation. simple rules can lead to heterogenous, chaotic, and random outcomes
* insurance modeling and actuarial science. catastrophic scenarios can have materially different outcomes than incrementally better or worse outcomes. In gambling, insurance, or finance, this is known as getting wiped out.
* how can our unique worldviews and its incorporation in our investing affect the outcomes of our investments? markets are complex adaptive systems that change based on the positions that being taken.
* roleplay is a strength of agents, how effective can agents be at roleplaying entities like the strait of hormuz? pax historia (yc startup) has an interactive alternative history simulation sandbox realized through agent simulation. aaru and simile are startups that use agent societies to simulate answers to market research and other sociopolitical questions.
* design language and UI/UX: visual programming, graphify/visualizers of nodes and edges/ontology visualizers, simulation games/auto-battlers/(maybe) dwarf fortress + rimworld, compositionality/category theory
* expanding on how compositionality could be applied here: certain approximations will be needed to be made to make prediction and forecasting of complex dynamics tractable, however, the same way that a chess engine can be made more accurate by asking it to search deeper lines of play, a forecast or world model simulation can be made by refining and increasing the resolution of the components that make up any particular entity. e.g. modeling a u.s. election based on an average makeup of the us vs modeling state by state vs simulating counties within each state
* heaviside and dirac delta function for modeling discrete impulses and phenomena in physics versus continuous inputs. kalman filters for isolating signals?
* impeccable style?
